I've started two parallel jobs: one maps how the codebase is wired today (frontend, server, Mastra agents, any storage), and one checks current docs for Better Auth, Supabase, Clerk, Convex and Mastra Memory. I'll come back with a recommendation and a few questions once both finish.

**First, about the AWS details you pasted:** your console password and CLI access key and secret are now in this chat. I won't use or store them. Since this is a shared $25 allowance, please rotate them soon. In IAM, open your user, go to Security credentials, deactivate that access key and create a new one. Change the console password too if you can. When we deploy, the keys should go in your local `~/.aws/credentials` or an IAM role on the EC2 instance, never in the repo or chat.

One constraint shapes the whole plan already: your AWS allowance only covers **EC2, Lambda, IAM and load balancers**. That means no managed AWS database (RDS, DynamoDB) and no Cognito for login. So the data layer will be one of:
- a SQLite file on the one EC2 instance;
- Postgres in Docker on that instance;
- a free hosted service such as Supabase, Neon or Turso.

